-The active C++ slice is now a **ResumeTransfer work-order planner**. Rev0684 could execute `MaterializeStagedFile` and `CleanupCommittedStaging`, but partial or missing staged content still stopped at a read-only action label. Rev0685 adds `plan_sync_session_checkpoint_resume_transfers`, which consumes the restart action router, selects missing chunks under request/peer budgets, and emits peer-bound work-order evidence with `sync-resume-transfer-request:v1:`, `sync-resume-peer-request:v1:`, and `sync-resume-peer-schedule:v1:` keys.
+The active C++ slice is now a **ResumeTransfer fake-peer executor**. Rev0685 emitted peer-bound transfer work orders, but those work orders were still inert. Rev0686 adds `execute_sync_session_checkpoint_resume_transfer_workorders`, which consumes the rev0685 planner, reads selected chunks from the verified source tree, writes/reuses DB-bound staged chunk evidence, upserts checkpoint receipt rows as `accepted`, advances file/session transfer counters, and then re-runs the action router so completed staged evidence becomes `MaterializeStagedFile`.
 
